# Command oiq

## What does this command do:

Fast, open-source tool for estimating infrastructure costs from Terraform plans and state files

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/terrateamio/openinfraquote/releases/download/v1.10.0/oiq-linux-amd64-v1.10.0.tar.gz -o /tmp/oiq.tar.gz && tar -xzf /tmp/oiq.tar.gz -C /tmp && chmod +x /tmp/oiq && mv /tmp/oiq ~/.local/bin/oiq && rm /tmp/oiq.tar.gz
For Raspberry Pi install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/terrateamio/openinfraquote/releases/download/v1.10.0/oiq-linux-arm64-v1.10.0.tar.gz -o /tmp/oiq.tar.gz && tar -xzf /tmp/oiq.tar.gz -C /tmp && chmod +x /tmp/oiq && mv /tmp/oiq ~/.local/bin/oiq && rm /tmp/oiq.tar.gz
For Mac install using: brew tap terrateamio/openinfraquote && brew install openinfraquote

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/oiq
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.local/bin/oiq
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/oiq

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/terrateamio/openinfraquote

## Command options

# Before first use — download the pricing sheet:
curl -s https://oiq.terrateam.io/prices.csv.gz | gunzip > prices.csv

# Full workflow: match resources then price them
tofu show -json tfplan.json | oiq match --pricesheet prices.csv | oiq price
tofu show -json tfplan.json | oiq match -p prices.csv | oiq price --format markdown
tofu show -json tfplan.json | oiq match -p prices.csv | oiq price --region us-east-1

# Save match output to file, then price separately
oiq match --pricesheet prices.csv --output match.json plan.json
oiq price --input match.json --format json

# Output formats: summary (default), text, json, markdown, atlantis-comment
oiq price --input match.json --format atlantis-comment

# Filter by region using match-query
oiq price --input match.json --mq 'region = us-east-1'

# Provide a usage file (for resources billed by usage, e.g. data transfer)
oiq price --input match.json --usage usage.yaml

# Print the default usage file as a starting template
oiq print-default-usage

# Environment variables
# OIQ_PRICE_SHEET  — path to pricing CSV (replaces --pricesheet)
# OIQ_REGION       — region to price against (replaces --region)
# OIQ_OUTPUT_FORMAT — output format (replaces --format)
